opening a conversation, making small talk. Hey, I like those pants, those are good-looking shoes. What do you think of the weather today? How long have you been riding this train? Nick says there are two steps to having a pleasant conversation, getting it started and keeping it going. And what we find in our data is that the barrier seems to be in the first of those things. It's not that people anticipate that having a conversation once it gets going will be unpleasant.
开启对话，进行闲聊。嘿，我喜欢那条裤子，那双鞋很好看。你觉得今天的天气怎么样？你坐这趟火车多久了？尼克说，进行愉快的谈话有两个步骤：开始谈话和保持谈话。我们在数据中发现，障碍似乎在于第一步。并不是人们预料到一旦谈话开始就会不愉快。

