They think that'll be okay. Instead, the barrier seems to come earlier. There's anxiety about actually starting the conversation, engaging in the conversation. And that's what seems to lead people to predict that it's going to be unpleasant. Nick has an analogy. It's like climbing up a steep hill.
他们认为那会没问题。相反，障碍似乎来得更早。对于真正开始谈话、参与谈话存在焦虑。而这似乎导致人们预测谈话会不愉快。尼克有一个类比。这就像爬上一座陡峭的山。

