00:42:21.000 --> 00:43:06.000
You've got to get over that initial speed bump at the top and then after that it seems to go pretty smoothly but if you don't get over that first initial bump you'll never get started. Of course not everyone has the same freedom to chat with strangers in the way Nick suggests. Agenda, race, appearance and many other factors affect how people view us. In some context it can be dangerous to start a conversation with a stranger. But what's clear from many of the messages we receive from hidden brain listeners is that the desire for connection is deep and in many cases, unfulfilled. Loneliness and social isolation has become more and more part of my daily life.
你必须越过顶部的初始减速带，然后在那之后一切似乎进行得相当顺利，但如果你没有越过第一个初始障碍，你就永远无法开始。当然，并不是每个人都有同样的自由以尼克建议的方式与陌生人聊天。性别、种族、外貌和许多其他因素影响着人们如何看待我们。在某些情况下，与陌生人开始谈话可能是危险的。但从我们收到的许多“隐藏大脑”（Hidden Brain）听众的留言中可以清楚地看出，对联系的渴望是深刻的，在许多情况下，是未被满足的。孤独和社会孤立已经越来越多地成为我日常生活的一部分。

